# Pin the fleet-served slave agent + its downloadable artifact to LF so the
# versions.json sha256 is deterministic across checkouts/OSes. Without this a
# Windows (CRLF) checkout hashes differently from the committed LF blob, so the
# manifest sha mismatches what a clean checkout / Linux deploy serves and the
# fleet auto-update sha-check fails (see docs panel-artifact-serving notes).
/slave-agent/slave_agent.py text eol=lf
/artifacts/slave-agent.py text eol=lf
/sidecar-agent/sidecar_agent.py text eol=lf
/client-agent/client_agent.py text eol=lf
/client-agent/leikwan_mptcp_client.py text eol=lf
/artifacts/leikwan-mptcp-client.py text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the browser assets of the web skin: skin_v2_legacy_freeze_test.php
# freezes the legacy skin's stylesheets and signal-chamber.js by sha256, and a
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would hash CRLF bytes and fail the freeze with
# a mismatch that is not evidence of an edit.
#
# Scoped to that one directory rather than a repo-wide *.css / *.js, which would
# also normalise the Tauri client sources and the vendored trees this migration
# has no business touching. Scoped to the directory rather than the four frozen
# filenames so that adding a file to the freeze list does not silently need a
# second edit here -- the freeze test asserts every path it hashes is covered by
# a pin below, so the two cannot drift apart.
#
# Deleted with the legacy skin in the teardown commit (Task 16).
/master/public/assets/*.css text eol=lf
/master/public/assets/*.js text eol=lf
